#!/usr/bin/env sh
# peaks-loop commit gate. Design + why-it-is-a-ratchet: .husky/peaks-gate.mjs
#
# Staged files only: a file you touch may not get worse, and a file that did
# not exist before must be clean outright. Files you did not touch are exempt,
# because 1178 of 1266 are currently unformatted and blocking on those would
# block every commit from the first one.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
#   - tsc        whole-program; it cannot be scoped to a file list, so a
#                single-file commit would pay for the entire repo anyway.
#                It runs in CI: `npm run build` in .github/workflows/ci.yml
#                does the canonical typecheck (`tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`).
#                (This line said "it runs in the push gate" until slice B5,
#                2026-09-23. That was true then and is false now: the push
#                gate checks only the files being pushed, and no longer runs
#                a whole-program tsc.)
#   - unit tests ~7 min; CI runs the full suite in the `vitest + build` job.
#                The push gate runs only the tests the pushed diff implies
#                (`pnpm test:changed`, see .husky/pre-push).
#   - formatting OUTSIDE the lint scope. `pnpm format:check` covers src, tests,
#                packages and scripts; this hook compares only the owner-decided
#                lint scope (src/** + packages/*/src/**, .husky/lint-scope.mjs,
#                owner decision 2026-10-03) and says so by name for every staged
#                file it drops ("outside the lint scope, not compared").
#                THE TWO SCOPES ARE MEANT TO BE DIFFERENT, and until rid-038 the
#                reason was written down nowhere. This hook is a PER-FILE RATCHET
#                ("a file you touch may not be worse than its own baseline row"),
#                so it can only cover files that HAVE a baseline row — the owned
#                product boundary. Widening the ratchet to tests/** + scripts/**
#                would re-open an owner decision, need rows for ~600 more files,
#                and refuse every commit touching an already-unformatted file
#                (an absent row reads as NEW FILE, which must be clean outright).
#                So the wide check is NOT narrowed to match this hook: it is
#                EXECUTED, in the `format-check` job of .github/workflows/ci.yml,
#                as .husky/format-check-ratchet.mjs. That job is ALSO a ratchet —
#                the current unformatted set must stay INSIDE a named baseline SET
#                of 12 files (it may only shrink) over the SAME four globs this
#                hook does not cover. So the
#                two are consistent on the only axis that matters here ("ratchet,
#                never a whole-repo boolean"); they differ in WHICH files they
#                watch, not in what KIND of check they are. Before rid-038 no
#                executor called the wide check at all, and unformatted files
#                reached a commit with every gate green.
set -e
pnpm exec lint-staged
